                <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">Recovery happens. That is the part of a theft story that is easy to miss. In late August 2026, Middleborough Police Department detectives announced that all 15 firearms stolen in a July 25 breaking and entering had been recovered — some of them after a federal search warrant in another state.</p>

                <p>This is not a rewrite of the after-theft steps. If a firearm is already gone, start with <a href="stolen-firearm-checklist.html" class="text-av-gold hover:underline">What to Do When a Firearm Is Stolen</a>. This post is about what happens if those guns come back — and why matching them to an owner is a records problem, not a recovery problem.</p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold text-gray-900">Middleborough, then Cold Brook: all 15 recovered</h2>
                <p>On July 25, 2026, fifteen firearms were stolen in a breaking and entering in Middleborough, Massachusetts. According to an <a href="https://middleboroughpolice.com/2026/08/25/middleborough-detectives-lead-investigation-resulting-in-recovery-of-15-stolen-firearms/" class="text-av-gold hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">August 25 release</a> from the Middleborough Police Department, detectives investigated with the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives — including the ATF Bridgewater and Syracuse field offices — and other law enforcement partners. <a href="https://wbsm.com/middleboro-15-stolen-firearms-recovered-arrest/" class="text-av-gold hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WBSM</a> reported the same recovery, citing that release.</p>

                <p>Detectives identified James Delano, a convicted felon, as a suspect.</p>

                <p>On July 28, 2026, investigators executed a state search warrant at Delano's Middleborough residence. They seized ammunition and his cell phone.</p>

                <p>The investigation then led to a residence in Cold Brook, New York, belonging to members of Delano's family. On August 13, ATF agents from the Bridgewater and Syracuse field offices executed a federal search warrant there. They recovered five of the stolen firearms, plus ammunition that had been buried in a wooded area near the residence.</p>

                <p>Further interviews in Cold Brook recovered the other ten stolen firearms and more ammunition.</p>

                <p>All 15 stolen firearms were recovered.</p>

                <p>The U.S. Attorney's Office for the District of Massachusetts charged Delano with being a felon in possession of ammunition. He has been apprehended. Additional charges remain under consideration.</p>

                <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-6 my-8">
